// THE SLOT a packaged script is written into. The build ships it EMPTY (payload.bin is a 0-byte file), and
// `tools/slc-pack.slc` fills the same type+name pair with a script's text or a .slcbc's bytes via
// BeginUpdateResourceW/UpdateResourceW. The launcher reads it with FindResourceW(RT_RCDATA, "SLCPAYLOAD"),
// and size 0 ("not packaged") is a state it has to be able to see, which is why the entry exists at all.
SLCPAYLOAD RCDATA "payload.bin"